mode: "100644"
text: "# Templates & worked examples\n\n## The two-column AV script (the production document)\n| AUDIO (heard) | VISUAL (seen) |\n|---|---|\n| [VO] \"Most invoices get paid late for one reason.\" | Punch-in on face; text pop: \"one reason\" |\n| [VO] \"It's not the client. It's the due date you chose.\" | B-roll: calendar close-up; [SFX] tick |\n| [Dialogue] \"Here's the fix — net-7, not net-30.\" | Back to face, medium; prop: printed invoice |\n| [VO] CTA: \"Full breakdown in the caption.\" | End card, brand template; loop frame matches open |\nRule: no cell in the VISUAL column may read \"me talking\" twice in a row.\n\n## The shot-table storyboard (no drawing required)\n| # | Beat | On screen | Camera | Setup |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Hook | Face, punch-in | MCU, eye-level | A (desk, key light) |\n| 2 | Claim | Calendar B-roll | CU, top-down | B (tabletop) |\n| 3 | Fix | Face + prop | MS | A |\n| 4 | CTA/loop | End card | — | post |\n\n## The batch-shoot regroup (by setup, not by video)\nList every shot from all scripts → sort by SETUP column → shoot order: all Setup-A shots (every video's\ntalking segments), then all Setup-B (tabletop B-roll), then outfit-swap set. Per-shot checklist ticked on the\nday; buffer takes on every hook; footage labeled `vid#-shot#` for the edit map.\n\n## The AI-previz brief (per panel)\n\"Panel 4: [character bible — 3-5 lines + ref image]. Action: [one action]. Setting: [where]. Light: [when/\nmood]. Camera: [explicit — 'close-up on hands']. Palette: [brand hex/tone]. No-gos: [props/claims not to\nshow].\" One panel per generation; micro-beats for complex moments; directional, not final art.\n\n## The timing pass (before anything is shot)\nRead aloud, stopwatch running → words ÷ 140 wpm ≈ minutes → add pause/B-roll seconds → over target? Collapse\nthe middle beats, keep hook/payoff/loop → re-read → lock.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (the batch)\n\"scripted six videos monday. old me would've filmed six separate times. new me sorted 31 shots by setup: 18 at\nthe desk, 9 tabletop, 4 outside. shot all of it wednesday, 2.5 hours including coffee. the edit was fast\nbecause every clip was already named vid3-shot2. the shot list isn't admin — it's the whole trick.\" — regroup\nby setup, labeled handoff.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (the AV rescue)\n\"Our videos were lovely words and a very still face. So we rewrote one script in two columns and made a gentle\nrule: the visual column can't say 'me talking' twice in a row. Suddenly the receipts, the calendar, the mug —\nthey all had jobs. Same words, twice the watch time. One small step: take your last script and just add the\nsecond column.\" — the words-only fix, kindly.\n\n## Never\nShip a words-only script for a visual medium · storyboard as art instead of decisions · shoot without a\nnumbered shot list · film video-by-video when setups could batch · skip the stopwatch timing pass · stage\n'candid' moments as real · lift another creator's script (structure study only) · burn video credits before\npreviz frames · claim the agent can see footage or operate a camera.\n"
